===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A small [[animal]]. {{defdate|16th|20th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1929|author=Sir Arthur Conan Doyle|authorlink=Arthur Conan Doyle|title=When the World Screamed|url=http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks01/0100031h.html|passage='Is it not evident that if a parasitic '''animalcule''' desired to call its attention it would sink a hole in its shell and so stimulate its sensory apparatus?'}}
# A [[microscopic]] aquatic animal or [[protozoan]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=John Jeremiah Sullivan|title=Pulphead|passage=If we are part of nature, then we are synonymous with it at the metaphysical level, every bit as much as the first all-but-inorganic '''animalcules''' that ever formed a chain of themselves in the blow hole of a primordial sea vent.}}
# {{lb|en|now|historical}} A [[spermatozoon]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* '''2001''', David M Friedman, ''A Mind of its Own'', Robert Hale 2009, p. 60:
#*: Inside the '''animalcules''' in the thickest part of the semen he saw ‘all manner of great and small vessels […].’

